Infantry AI is licensed per directory. Copyright (c) SuperiorSoft LLC.

MPL-2.0 (the abstraction layer, the generic engine everything plugs into):
  superiorSoftLibrary/infantryProtocol, infantryCore, infantryRunner, infantry
  and the reserved, empty plugins/core/.
Apache-2.0 (everything concrete on top): every other directory, including the whole plugin
  API and plugin host (infantryPlugins), infantryBoard, the daemon and harness SDKs, the UI
  core, the apps, samples/, plugins/, docs/, docker/, scripts/, gradle/, .github/ and the
  root build files.
Neither license: the name "Infantry AI", the logo and the emblem (assets/branding and the copies
  in the app resources). They are trademarks of SuperiorSoft LLC; see docs/legal/TRADEMARK.md.

Each file names its license in an SPDX-License-Identifier header. Each MPL module and each Apache
top directory has its own LICENSE file; the full texts are in LICENSES/MPL-2.0.txt and
LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt. The authoritative map is docs/LICENSE-MAP.md (explained in
docs/wiki/licensing.md). Third-party components keep their own licenses: see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.

Outside code contributions are not accepted until the CLA is official (see CONTRIBUTING.md).
